1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,410
After the war, Australia decided it needed people.

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:05,870
The slogan was populate or perish.

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:10,310
Migrants arrived from Britain, Italy, Greece, the Netherlands

4
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,760
and beyond and millions have come since.

5
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,910
Many built the snowy mountain scheme, a massive

6
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:19,880
hydroelectric project using workers from over 30 countries.

7
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:23,550
But this era also holds deep pain.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:27,540
For decades, governments removed Aboriginal and Torres Strait

9
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:30,050
Islander children from their families.

10
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,080
They are known as the stolen generations.

11
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:34,590
Change came through struggle.

12
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:38,880
In 1966, Vincent Lingiari led the Gurindji people

13
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:41,550
off Wave Hill cattle station in a strike

14
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,000
for wages and land.

15
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:47,090
In 1967, over 90% of Australians voted yes

16
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:50,190
in a referendum to count Aboriginal people in

17
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,880
the census and let the Commonwealth make laws

18
00:00:52,930 --> 00:00:53,530
for them.

19
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:56,190
It's still the biggest yes vote in Australian

20
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:57,550
referendum history.

21
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,850
And remember the Prime Minister who vanished?

22
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,910
December 1967, Prime Minister Harold Holt went swimming

23
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,360
in rough surf near Melbourne and was never

24
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:08,130
found.

25
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,550
The country's tribute?

26
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,250
They named a swimming pool after him.

27
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,130
In 1973, the Sydney Opera House opened.

28
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,760
Its Danish architect Jorn Utzon had quit the

29
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:21,830
project years earlier and never saw it finished

30
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:22,750
in person.

31
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,370
The white Australia policy was fully dismantled in

32
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,950
the 1970s.

33
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,570
And in 1975, the Governor General dismissed Prime

34
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:35,510
Minister Gough Whitlam, the most dramatic constitutional crisis

35
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,110
in the nation's history.
